README.rst has the latest information on how to build and install Nsound.

The Python module needs Python 3.10 or newer and a C++20 compiler:

    python3 -m pip install Nsound       # from PyPI
    python3 -m pip install .            # from a source checkout

Plotting needs matplotlib:

    python3 -m pip install matplotlib

The C++ library, programs and unit tests build with Bazel
(https://bazel.build) on Linux, macOS and Windows:

    bazel build //...
    bazel test //...

On Windows, run .\setup-windows.ps1 from a PowerShell window first, it
installs Bazel and the Visual Studio C++ Build Tools, and turns on Developer
Mode and long paths, which the Python tests need for their symlinks and deep
paths.
